cloudflare-model-host bundles no third-party code. Its emitted JavaScript imports only Node.js built-in modules and,
for manifest validation, browser-model-manager from the same repository.

npm installs these dependencies separately, each under its own licence; none of their code is copied into this
package:
- cf (Cloudflare's command line), which the Cloudflare commands (origin-deploy, mirror-deploy, publish) run;
- vite and @cloudflare/vite-plugin, which the shipped cloudflare.config.ts and vite.config.ts import when cf builds
  the optional Cloudflare Workers.
The generic static-hosting commands (stage, verify, qualify-origin, warm) do not use them.

The model bytes it stages are not part of this package; their terms are recorded per model (see the README's
"Model terms").
